{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000001", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Overview and definition", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 1, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. From sensing to retirement: how data is born, processed, stored, and aged out across fog tiers. Data in fog systems moves through a lifecycle: capture at sensors, transport to the fog tier, in-flight processing (filter, enrich, aggregate), short-term hot storage on fog nodes, selective promotion of summaries and exceptions to the cloud, cold archival for compliance, and eventual retirement under retention policy. Hot data lives close and briefly; warm summaries live longer upstream; cold archives are cheap and distant. Retention policies and data minimization rules decide what survives each transition.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Overview and concept inventory", "code": "J({topic:__TOPIC__.name,concepts:__TOPIC__.concepts,count:__TOPIC__.concepts.length});assert(__TOPIC__.concepts.length>=5,'concepts');", "verified_output": "{\"topic\":\"Fog Data Lifecycle\",\"concepts\":[\"capture and ingest\",\"hot/warm/cold tiers\",\"data promotion\",\"summarization\",\"retention policies\",\"data lineage\",\"aging and eviction\",\"compliance holds\",\"cold archival\",\"retirement\"],\"count\":10}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000002", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Input and output contract", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 3, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Inputs: raw captures, retention policies, storage tier capacities, compliance rules. Outputs: lifecycle plan, tiered storage layout, retention schedule, lineage log.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Input/output contract validation", "code": "const req={workload_id:'wl-1',fog_node:'fog-1',deadline_ms:20,payload_kb:64};const ok=req.workload_id&&req.fog_node&&req.deadline_ms>0&&req.payload_kb<=1024;J({request:req,valid:!!ok});assert(ok,'contract');", "verified_output": "{\"request\":{\"workload_id\":\"wl-1\",\"fog_node\":\"fog-1\",\"deadline_ms\":20,\"payload_kb\":64},\"valid\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000003", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Core concepts", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 5, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Core concepts: capture and ingest; hot/warm/cold tiers; data promotion; summarization; retention policies; data lineage; aging and eviction; compliance holds; cold archival; retirement.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Core operation executed", "code": "// core: lifecycle transition simulation with retention eviction\nconst items=[{id:'raw-1',age_h:30,tier:'hot'},{id:'sum-1',age_h:2000,tier:'warm'},{id:'arc-1',age_h:20000,tier:'cold'},{id:'raw-2',age_h:5,tier:'hot'}];\nconst policy={hot:24,warm:2160,cold:26280};\nconst after=items.map(it=>{const limit=policy[it.tier];return {...it,retired:it.age_h>limit};});\nconst retired=after.filter(i=>i.retired).length;\nJ({items:items.length,retired,alive:after.length-retired});assert(retired===1,'one retired');assert(after.find(i=>i.id==='raw-2'&&!i.retired),'hot alive');", "verified_output": "{\"items\":4,\"retired\":1,\"alive\":3}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000004", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Worked example", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 7, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Traffic cameras: raw video is hot on roadside fog for 24 hours, 1-minute flow summaries stay warm for 90 days, and incident clips are archived cold for 3 years; everything else is evicted.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Worked example end to end", "code": "// end-to-end: 1000 raw events -> summaries -> what survives\nconst raw=1000;const hot_kept=raw;const summarized=Math.ceil(raw/60);const promoted=Math.ceil(summarized*0.1);\nJ({raw_events:raw,hot_window_kept:hot_kept,summaries:summarized,promoted_to_cloud:promoted,reduction_pct:+(100*(1-promoted/raw)).toFixed(1)});assert(promoted===2,'promotion');", "verified_output": "{\"raw_events\":1000,\"hot_window_kept\":1000,\"summaries\":17,\"promoted_to_cloud\":2,\"reduction_pct\":99.8}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000005", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Safety, limits, and failure modes", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 9, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Fog hot storage is small; aggressive summarization can destroy forensic detail; retention policy errors can delete evidence or keep liability.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Safety limits enforced", "code": "const CAP=10n**15n;const request=1000n;const over=CAP+1n;const ok1=request<=CAP;const ok2=over<=CAP;const node={cpu:8,used:7};const job={cpu:4};const fits=node.used+job.cpu<=node.cpu;J({generator_cap:'10^15 (one quadrillion)',request_ok:ok1,over_cap_refused:!ok2,oversized_job_refused:!fits});assert(ok1&&!ok2&&!fits,'limits');", "verified_output": "{\"generator_cap\":\"10^15 (one quadrillion)\",\"request_ok\":true,\"over_cap_refused\":true,\"oversized_job_refused\":true}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000006", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Beginner teaching exercise", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 2, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Start simple: define the fog computing stack (device, fog, cloud tiers) for Fog Data Lifecycle, identify which tier each workload belongs on, and verify with a small latency-budget calculation before scaling up.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Beginner teaching exercise: cloud vs fog round trip", "code": "const fog=T.nodes[0].rtt_ms;const cloud=T.cloud_rtt_ms;const saved=cloud-fog;const pct=Math.round(100*saved/cloud);J({fog_rtt_ms:fog,cloud_rtt_ms:cloud,saved_ms:saved,saving_pct:pct});assert(saved>0,'saves');assert(pct>50,'big win');", "verified_output": "{\"fog_rtt_ms\":5,\"cloud_rtt_ms\":125,\"saved_ms\":120,\"saving_pct\":96}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
{"id": "JAH-FOG-DATALIFE-000007", "slug": "fog-data-lifecycle", "title": "Fog Data Lifecycle \u2014 Advanced pattern", "edition": "public", "src": "public-harvest", "built_by": "assistant-built", "record_kind": "fog data science database record", "ladder_rank": 11, "body": "Public edition. Public fog data science knowledge, fact-checked reference. Advanced use of Fog Data Lifecycle combines neighboring topics: feed its outputs into the next tier, add verification checkpoints at each handoff, and automate the pipeline once the manual path is proven.", "concepts": ["capture and ingest", "hot/warm/cold tiers", "data promotion", "summarization", "retention policies", "data lineage", "aging and eviction", "compliance holds", "cold archival", "retirement"], "demo": {"language": "javascript", "title": "Advanced pattern: weighted failover across fog nodes", "code": "const nodes=T.nodes.map(n=>({...n,load:0}));let dropped=0;for(let i=0;i<40;i++){const live=nodes.filter(n=>n.load<n.cpu*10);if(!live.length){dropped++;continue;}const n=live.reduce((a,b)=>(a.load/a.cpu)<=(b.load/b.cpu)?a:b);n.load++;}const loads=nodes.map(n=>n.load);const over=nodes.filter(n=>n.load>n.cpu*10);const shares=nodes.map(n=>({id:n.id,share:+(n.load/n.cpu).toFixed(2)}));J({assigned:40-dropped,dropped,loads,shares,over_capacity:over.length});assert(dropped===0,'no drops');assert(over.length===0,'capacity');", "verified_output": "{\"assigned\":40,\"dropped\":0,\"loads\":[20,20],\"shares\":[{\"id\":\"fog-1\",\"share\":2.5},{\"id\":\"fog-2\",\"share\":2.5}],\"over_capacity\":0}", "verified_at": "2026-10-21", "node": "v24.20.0", "run": "node"}, "provenance": {"source_order": "manons-orders-2026-10-20-database-batch.txt item 89 (fog data science)", "last_verified": "2026-10-21", "origin": "assistant-built"}, "million_march": {"target": 1000000, "records_now": 8, "status": "march-in-progress"}, "generator": {"hard_cap": 1000000000000000, "ladder": ["simple", "competitive", "mix-and-match", "unmade", "top-notch-or-better", "future-grade", "god-mode"], "self_regulation": true, "stop_when_complete": true}, "ai": {"name": "JAH Fog Data Lifecycle Librarian", "scope": "archive-aware", "assistant_maker": true}, "links": {"related": ["fog-computing-architecture", "fog-edge-analytics", "fog-security-privacy", "fog-data-science-master"], "sibling_edition": "fog-data-lifecycle-signature"}}
